#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105602 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105745 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "97cd9132-458b-5234-a3d2-22b633acb74c" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing an Augmented Matrix for a Singular 2x2 System to REF and Solving the Resulting System"}] :question/id #uuid "7bfabbd2-9988-5c0e-9c17-3d430b3e7a0f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4699" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n![](images/97/9773630254747a4bbd072bd44a6263bdd078fa09005b1bb5f51c48b894d67daf.svg)\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n![](images/43/43b9b089e0f93e63acf386bb605a0e3751cc8660899ce19d23835f9f79918bcc.svg)\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y = 0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx - 3y = 1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=1+3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n![](images/4a/4a598a80f2f14715d1f10d182b3f80887c7586beabecc2a329119b624c19a4fa.svg)\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1+3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=⟨1+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105603 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "07f2ae4c-ff07-5b99-a7b0-90f460081eef" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Singular 2x2 System of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/id #uuid "681fce57-6be7-5907-b575-8c34b4819ae5" :question/math-academy-id "e-4700" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n![](images/bc/bcbd79c8cac28ef6bb4dc07a04789692d9726df238b4907841825244432c5783.svg)\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n![](images/d3/d381e04f0a7eb2973e20c9f397ef2e2267f90ac6992cfacd3a8927b4d48138a9.svg)\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{5}{2} & 2 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{5}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n![](images/89/89ca081f99d8cbd33bb11e58ef6aa91aa3045a02ff06c9877a53b9e2f88874db.svg)\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=-8$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=-8,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266012 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "07f2ae4c-ff07-5b99-a7b0-90f460081eef" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Singular 2x2 System of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04406210-94a5-519d-b563-c1787d94b573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2y-1 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263037} {:answer/id #uuid "20136c69-8c25-5eeb-a342-b87289d36eda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2-y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263293} {:answer/id #uuid "2dd5fd9e-9a95-5bbe-b9ca-15b27ae75731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263386} {:answer/id #uuid "742c670e-1f11-5451-982a-0b676be9c761" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2y-1 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264011} {:answer/id #uuid "b006db61-2f57-5349-bc2a-2f6efb0cae8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1-2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2dd5fd9e-9a95-5bbe-b9ca-15b27ae75731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263386} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ff41cad-65a8-5c50-a758-f7388a3a1397" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265366}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "df63ef93-068d-5156-97ea-60671ff0c81c" :question/math-academy-id "q-130923" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=-1 \\\\ -4x+8y &=7.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 8 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 8 & 7\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y &=3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=3$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=3,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288009 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "07f2ae4c-ff07-5b99-a7b0-90f460081eef" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Singular 2x2 System of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47c97c9a-b257-58e1-b8f0-fedf81973715" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2+4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285449} {:answer/id #uuid "6572eab8-0051-57e0-9e01-2a886e1ff7f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2-4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285709} {:answer/id #uuid "7fb0f231-ef58-570a-a217-3ac725a9c673" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1+4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285962} {:answer/id #uuid "a610291f-fe71-59f4-ba82-34c306fd05eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286302} {:answer/id #uuid "df55ab77-72af-5c93-956c-d075379dc2c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2+4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286824}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6572eab8-0051-57e0-9e01-2a886e1ff7f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2-4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285709} :answer-field/id #uuid "613521d7-e573-530c-9e5e-83c95de64ea2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e9e4d803-6c25-5024-8fca-536e9832cf45" :question/math-academy-id "q-20783" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+4y &=2 \\\\ 2x+8y &=4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+4y &=2 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+4y=2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=2-4y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2-4y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2-4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390388 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105745 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "97cd9132-458b-5234-a3d2-22b633acb74c" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing an Augmented Matrix for a Singular 2x2 System to REF and Solving the Resulting System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9973610-47f9-5f62-a4ae-54d727ff19bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1-2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390390} {:answer/id #uuid "c2ddc9c8-cf3c-5347-a18e-5fc3f7cd82d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2-4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390391} {:answer/id #uuid "4142878a-1989-59e7-bb13-e08f2f47a895" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2-4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390392} {:answer/id #uuid "15cec20b-2ee9-50b2-83e8-5d388cb51a75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1-2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390393} {:answer/id #uuid "2cc15e06-5b06-530d-86f3-88d4d6831e6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1+2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9973610-47f9-5f62-a4ae-54d727ff19bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1-2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390390} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c5b0769-2362-5bb9-8ad0-cec516d68985" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390389}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f0787607-5bca-5e97-b7f4-40db59c2425f" :question/math-academy-id "q-20963" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 8 & 16 & -8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 8 & 16 & -8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-8){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+2y=-1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-1-2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-1-2y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1-2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106313 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105745 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "97cd9132-458b-5234-a3d2-22b633acb74c" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing an Augmented Matrix for a Singular 2x2 System to REF and Solving the Resulting System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9f1382a-870c-5f7c-b007-6684dc65136e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1 - 2y, y⟩, y ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104027} {:answer/id #uuid "e68d6a57-2fff-5fe1-97e2-53e0d4e0fb15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1 + 2y, y⟩, y ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104028} {:answer/id #uuid "ee0db42e-1100-5418-8315-c630442bb8ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104029} {:answer/id #uuid "56c35cf2-8374-5cfd-8ca3-d7861125849e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - 1 + 2y, y⟩, y ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104030} {:answer/id #uuid "7ec12860-5f4a-5e06-8d80-fe18641609f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1, 0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104031}] :answer-field/id #uuid "a117e6ad-ea85-5ffa-be6d-c20de27fa2cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104026} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7b917a4-149a-5335-87b0-b5af432e1dd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379836} {:answer/id #uuid "d5fcad4a-a362-5ebf-bbea-e056e83246a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379837} {:answer/id #uuid "63ca10a3-6abf-594c-bc38-1b37ffcbdc38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1-2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379838} {:answer/id #uuid "1730136e-f78b-5eda-af0d-81956b5fce34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1+2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379839} {:answer/id #uuid "72d559c6-a1d1-5e3e-be26-d5a5b1c9e977" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1+2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1730136e-f78b-5eda-af0d-81956b5fce34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1+2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379839} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b446b32-d3dd-5edb-b643-a1c5a81e8d04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379835}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0407db63-d38b-50cb-b37f-dfd7ce1a8b10" :question/math-academy-id "q-42156" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=1 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-2y=1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=1+2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=1+2y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1+2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=⟨1+2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402782 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105745 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "97cd9132-458b-5234-a3d2-22b633acb74c" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing an Augmented Matrix for a Singular 2x2 System to REF and Solving the Resulting System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6429a97e-1ea2-5116-bdb0-c323c42ac6b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3-2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402784} {:answer/id #uuid "7529729a-7538-57b4-bb95-683aba7b3a43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3+2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402785} {:answer/id #uuid "0937d732-3e23-55bb-bb34-82a9a014fa2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3+2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402786} {:answer/id #uuid "3e199bd5-5ebe-5592-b9f0-829bfdc64fe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3-2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402787} {:answer/id #uuid "2f8c9956-92cc-5dc7-bdf2-6e23c0868904" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2-3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402788}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6429a97e-1ea2-5116-bdb0-c323c42ac6b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3-2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402784} :answer-field/id #uuid "e33c2e04-873c-5d06-b295-2871dc81bbfb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402783}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "41fb9598-c5d7-5a4e-b94b-50dacda69952" :question/math-academy-id "q-42158" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=3 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+2y=3.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=3-2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3-2y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3-2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=⟨3-2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329635 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "07f2ae4c-ff07-5b99-a7b0-90f460081eef" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Singular 2x2 System of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "124cd317-220b-5b1b-b0df-11ccb5699d8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7-4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327089} {:answer/id #uuid "36c238b2-e923-54d5-9366-3b0928bcfd68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4-7y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327411} {:answer/id #uuid "3b279e3a-1875-5863-9a8a-f83033667b33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6-9y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327452} {:answer/id #uuid "4c3ca48a-486f-5497-9863-4452db258c31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327597} {:answer/id #uuid "66bc3170-2988-5341-bdeb-88dc944a6924" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4+7y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36c238b2-e923-54d5-9366-3b0928bcfd68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4-7y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327411} :answer-field/id #uuid "a49ef358-bb1d-5f86-95ec-c04c91c0bf60" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329466}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2bf7b16f-c404-5080-a0f3-019c76bbad3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-42159" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+7y &=4 \\\\ 6x+42y &=24.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 42 & -24\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 42 & 24\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+7y &=4 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+7y=4.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=4-7y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=4-7y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4-7y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392488 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105745 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "97cd9132-458b-5234-a3d2-22b633acb74c" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing an Augmented Matrix for a Singular 2x2 System to REF and Solving the Resulting System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bce7c5fc-118d-57ed-b7b7-198ec9740ae2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2+4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392490} {:answer/id #uuid "d6d36658-bde5-5a80-bfa7-5f01e189d3c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-6+4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392491} {:answer/id #uuid "882a5fb0-4677-57cd-a0eb-b59850dc71e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6-4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392492} {:answer/id #uuid "8f92d555-2375-53e0-8687-b595e26d132d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6+4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392493} {:answer/id #uuid "aa8fa779-e3c8-583f-924d-8c09429656f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4+4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f92d555-2375-53e0-8687-b595e26d132d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6+4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392493} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ddc2483-85ad-5618-94ab-3e0c00d11533" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392489}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d49a7f92-7486-5a6e-9890-b6f6940d9011" :question/math-academy-id "q-42160" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 8 & -12\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 8 & -12\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-4y &=6 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-4y=6.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=6+4y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=6+4y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6+4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342079 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "07f2ae4c-ff07-5b99-a7b0-90f460081eef" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Singular 2x2 System of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35e6a7c5-5218-5d25-a8f6-7848a5bca3fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339610} {:answer/id #uuid "42fb3843-e811-598c-9cd8-40fa0350bea1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1+2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339713} {:answer/id #uuid "57cf24ad-e2ac-533d-8f71-64d4e595fa8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2-y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339928} {:answer/id #uuid "ad94e501-a2d3-5422-a57f-c8541c6ecb28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2+y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340708} {:answer/id #uuid "d21c64f6-9851-5d4c-8362-9495bc2b9f3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1-2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35e6a7c5-5218-5d25-a8f6-7848a5bca3fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339610} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0dcd427-5fab-5d80-85bc-c5c9b1007acd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341690}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b0b4636b-3357-5697-b846-0e6a1da3fd28" :question/math-academy-id "q-73751" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-10y &=-5 \\\\ 2x-4y &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -10 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -10 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y &=4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=4$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=4,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution."}]}
